# ── Build artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rust (src/agent/)
src/agent/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Go (src/control/) — compiled binaries and test/coverage output
src/control/merc
src/control/control
src/control/**/*.test
*.out
coverage.out
# Swift (clients/macapp/) build products
clients/macapp/.build/
# Assembled .app bundle from clients/macapp/assemble-app.sh (build output; rebuilt on demand)
build/
# Python (clients/sdk/) caches
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
clients/sdk/python/build/
clients/sdk/python/dist/
clients/sdk/python/*.egg-info/

# ── Local run artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ops/scripts/prove-local.sh writes its throwaway Postgres/MinIO data, logs, and the
# proof ledger under .artifacts/. Logs and pidfiles from any ad-hoc local runs.
# Never commit these.
.artifacts/
ops/scripts/*.log
*.log
*.pid

# ── Secrets / local config ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.bak*
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
.env.go-closure
.env.local
.secrets/
# The agent's runtime config holds a worker token — commit agent.example.toml,
# never the real one.
src/agent/agent.toml

# ── Editor / OS cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ── Design sources ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The layered logo master (clients/web/logo/cx_logo.psd, ~8 MB) is the editable brand source,
# kept local to keep clones lean. The flat source PNG + the flat masters
# (cx-mark-white, cx-app-icon) ARE committed; ops/scripts/cx_trace.py + cx_logo.py
# regenerate the metal render from the PNG. The full-res 1080px render master stays
# local (clients/web/logo/cx-metal*); the right-sized served copies live in clients/web/assets and ARE
# committed.
*.psd
clients/web/logo/cx-metal*

# ── PROTECTED ASSETS (SACRED — see BLACKHOLE.md) ─────────────────────────────
# Models, weights, datasets, and caches are expensive or impossible to
# regenerate. They are gitignored so they are NEVER committed, but they must
# NEVER be deleted or moved either: a user who pulled a model yesterday still
# has it working today. The collapse restructures the code that loads them, not
# the artifacts. Do not `git clean` these away.
models/
data/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin

# ── Render pixel artifacts (regenerable — kept local, never committed) ────────
# Every rendered PNG/JPG, cached .blend geometry, and calibration frame is
# regenerated by src/render/build_*.py from the committed builders + specs. The
# pixels bloated the repo to ~800 MB (a 105 MB foam cache even exceeded GitHub's
# 100 MB file limit), so ALL render images/binaries are stripped from history and
# ignored here. The TRAIL stays committed: the .py builders + .md reports/specs.
# Heavy binary artifacts (preview/verify PNGs, reference .pdf/.jpg datasheets, the
# .glb master) are relocated to the computexchange-render-lab pack (see
# PACK_MANIFESTS.json) — regenerate via the builders or hydrate from history.
src/render/**/*.png
src/render/**/*.jpg
src/render/**/*.jpeg
src/render/**/*.webp
src/render/**/*.exr
src/render/**/*.blend
src/render/**/*.blend1
src/render/**/*.glb
src/render/**/*.pdf
src/render/ref/**/*.svg
src/render/ref/**/*.rtf
src/render/cache/

# agent worktrees / local tooling
.claude/
clients/web/admin-demo.html

# rust crate build dirs (spec-engine, token-spec-poc, renderer)
target/

# python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# regenerable render diagnostics (pixel artifacts; the builders + ledgers are the trail)
diag_images/

# Benchmark research outputs (denoiser .pt/.onnx, spec-lab .jsonl ledgers, bench
# reports) are relocated to the computexchange-benchmarks pack (PACK_MANIFESTS.json).
# Not proof/CI/build bound. Regenerate via the bench/spec-lab drivers or hydrate.
docs/speed-lane-reports/
docs/bench-local-reports/

# pytest's discovery cache is generated at every repository depth. The claim and
# source-fingerprint scanners must never mistake it for a product document.
**/.pytest_cache/

# scratch output from cx audit --out
tmp/

# Local Go tool caches (src/agent/sandbox)
.gocache/
.gomodcache/
.gopath/

# patch(1) backups from applying delegated diffs
*.orig
*.rej

# TypeScript SDK build output and local deps
clients/sdk/typescript/dist/
clients/sdk/typescript/node_modules/

# Local canary credentials. Never commit.
.merc-credentials.env
.merc-runpod.env
.merc-secrets.env
# RunPod intent markers (create-before-bind trail) and other local pod state.
# Not evidence: a crash mid-run must not leave a committed spend claim.
.merc-runpod/

# Operator credential material under .tools — untracked; remains on disk for
# local use. Still present in git history and requires rotation by the operator.
.tools/rp-key/
# Wildcard so a newly introduced .merc-*.env cannot be committed by accident.
.merc-*.env
.merc-release/
.cloudflare-zone-backups/

# Checkpoint receipts are LOCAL gate artifacts bound to a commit hash, not repo
# evidence. Committing one would create a commit that itself has no receipt, and
# the pre-push hook would then refuse the very commit that carries the proof.
evidence/checkpoint/

# The single `go test -json` record `make ci` hands to the skip gate.
.ci-test.json
.ci-test.json.*

# serena MCP writes a per-project cache here; it is tooling state, not source.
.serena/

# wrangler local state (auth, build cache); never committed
.wrangler/

# Legacy local roots retained on disk after the canonical layout move.  They are
# runtime/build leftovers, not a second source tree; preserve them locally while
# keeping the tracked surface under src/, clients/, ops/, docs/, and evidence/.
/agent/
/control/
/pricing/
/render/
/deploy/
/scripts/
/web/
